=2 Walkthrough
Trade enough {p:Crystals} to the {p:Conquest NPC} to raise your Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the {n:Gate Guard}.
* Head to {z:Chateau d'Oraguille} and check the **Great Hall** door for a cutscene.
* Speak with {p:Rahal} (H-9, western door directly across from the entry way) to receive the {@k} {k:Crystal dowser} and further instructions.
* Head to the {z:Temple of Uggalepih} and farm a {@i:Prelate Key|1137} {i:Prelate Key|Prelate Key|1137} from the {m:Tonberry Stabbers|Tonberry Stabber} on Map 3/4.
** **See the note below before farming the key.** Alternatively you may farm {m:Tonberry Choppers|Tonberry Chopper} in the {z:Yhoator Jungle} or {m:Tonberry Slashers|Tonberry Slasher} in the {z:Den of Rancor}.
** Several {m:Tonberry Slashers|Tonberry Slasher} spawn in the large room near the {z:Den of Rancor} {p:Unity Warp} (Level 128).
* Make your way through the {z:Temple|Temple of Uggalepih} until you reach the door at (I-10) on Map 2, that can only be opened by killing the {m:Temple Guardian}.
** The {z:Temple of Uggalepih} {p:Geomagnetic Fount} is closest.
** Alternate Route: Take the Survival Guide to {z:Temple|Temple of Uggalepih}. Exit out to Yhoator Jungle. Go around the corner to entrance #3 back into the temple, and you will be on Map 2.
** The {m:Guardian|Temple Guardian} will not be there and the door will be open if someone has defeated it in the last 15 minutes.
* Pass into the big room, and head upstairs and through the door at (J-10) which requires the {@i:Prelate Key|1137} {i:Prelate Key|Prelate Key|1137}.
** **Note**: The door on top of the east set of stairs __can__ be bypassed without a {@i:Prelate Key|1137} {i:Prelate Key|Prelate Key|1137}. One way of doing this is summoning a {p:Trust} that moves away from you, such as {p:Yoran-Oran}, engaging an enemy in front of the door, and hoping that the Trust runs through the door. This is a much faster method than dealing with the low drop rate of the key.
** You only need 1 Prelate Key to open this door for yourself or an entire party. As soon as someone makes it behind this door they can open it for anyone else coming through.
* In the south hallway examine the three **???** in any order. From west to east, they are in the first (G-10), third (H-10), and fourth rooms (I-10). The fourth room has multiple **???**, ensure you get the message "Obtained key item: {k:Piece of a broken key}."
** Each **???** will provide a {@k} {k:Piece of a broken key}.
** Each player in the party must obtain the 3 {@k} {k:Piece of a broken key} in order to complete the final cutscene.
* After you have all 3 keys, select the second door (H-10) to spawn 2 {m:Doll} NMs: {m:Nio-Hum} and {m:Nio-A}.
** Both have around 6500 HP, do regular {m:Doll} attacks, and cannot be {p:slept|Sleep (Status)}.
** You may pull one at a time if {s:Sneak} is activated before spawning.
** The {m:Dolls|Doll} are aggressive to magic so you may not pull with magic.
* After the {m:Dolls|Doll} have been defeated, check the door again for a cutscene.
** This cutscene will detail that you failed to find the sword you came here for, it is the correct cutscene. You can warp out after this.
* Return to {z:Chateau d'Oraguille} and check the **Great Hall** door for a cutscene.
* You will be awarded Rank 9 and 80,000 {p:Gil}.

